import soundpass_gen as G

NOTE = '''0.3.53 (2026-11-01) = GEAR LANE ROUND 1 (gl1) - VANILLA GEAR AUDIT items 8.2 / 8.3 / 8.4 + the A2 ELEMENT POWER follow-up (FULL round: a
  one-time config update, item drops, recipes). research/Vanilla-Gear-Audit.md sections 2, 4, 6, 8; Skyy (docs/answered/gear.md 2026-10-30 VANILLA
  GEAR AUDIT, all 8 audit defaults taken): Q "UT / Mythic picks from unused vanilla weapons: Ancient Bronze Daggers + Sword = Z1 UT (Assassin /
  Warrior), Doomed = Z2 UT family, Saurian = Z4, Scythe_Void = Berserker Mythic, Silversteel = Warrior UT Z3-4, Katana = Warrior Z2 drop. OK?" ->
  "Yes, all of them (Recommended)"; Q7 default "use the 5 vanilla Bronze weapons and build only the missing families at T3".
  1. THE BRONZE WEAPON RUNG (audit gap 1, Z1 T3): vanilla Weapon_Sword / Spear / Shortbow / Staff / Daggers_Bronze (no vanilla recipe) get our
     standalone recipes SkyyGear_Recipe_<id> = the Iron item's recipe of the same family with the Iron Ingots swapped 1:1 for Bronze Ingots (the
     0.3.29 Bronze Mining rule; the staff = the 0.2 magic rule: the Iron shortbow's recipe; the spear = the Iron SWORD's - vanilla spears have
     none), the developer-only Armory bench entry dropped. They are PLAIN pieces (GearPack.combatId: metal word Bronze) = Smithing > Weapons
     (the benches refuse them like every plain piece), band level.material.Bronze 15-23, tag "T3 Bronze" (tools/tier_tags.py combat_tag: the
     id's metal word), sorted by tier on the Smithing tab. The other families (Axe, Battleaxe, Club, Mace, Longsword, Wand, Crossbow, Kunai,
     Spellbook, Bo, Fist) have NO Bronze item anywhere (Assets.zip + Skyy's Mods folder checked 2026-11-01): they are SkyyArmory's alloy
     ladder (its 0.1.34 Weapon_<family>_<metal>_SkyWynn builder) - left for a SkyyArmory round; SkyyGear already rolls / levels / crafts a
     Weapon_<family>_Bronze_SkyWynn id by its name (harness-checked: combatId + the Bronze band).
  2. SPEARS CRAFTABLE (audit gap 2): every vanilla plain-metal spear (Copper, Iron, Thorium, Cobalt, Adamantite, Mithril + Bronze above) gets a
     standalone recipe = that metal's SWORD recipe (Skyy's own HyMax pack used the same shape for the Mithril spear). The recipe file names
     the Weapon Bench (vanilla has no spear tab), but a spear is a PLAIN piece (GearPack.combatId), so the benches refuse it like every plain
     piece (0.3.37) - it is crafted ONLY through /smithing > Weapons > the Spear card. Onyxium has no plain recipe at any family (parked) - none. SkyyArmory's 8 zone-metal spears stay drop-only
     (its items; its round).
  3. UNTIERED FROM UNUSED VANILLA WEAPONS (tools/ut_vanilla.py, the 0.3.47 ut28 pipeline unchanged): 10 rows - 9 SkyyGear copies (the vanilla
     model by path + the orange placeholder recolour, the darker map where a 0.3.47 UT already wears that look) + 1 SkyyArmory row (the Doomed
     staff - SkyySkills ships its own Weapon_Staff_Doomed file, so SkyyArmory builds that copy; unusable until then, GearUt.ok):
     Z1 Barrow Fangs (Ancient Bronze Daggers, Assassin), Grovewarden's Relic (Ancient Bronze Sword, Warrior); Z2 the Doomed family: Dune Reaver
     (battleaxe, Berserker), Doomed Oath (sword, Warrior), Dunefang (fang daggers, Assassin), Dreadstring (shortbow, Archer), Doomcaller
     (staff, Mage - SkyyArmory); Z3 Everfrost Silverbrand (Silversteel, Warrior); Z4 Saurian Talons (daggers, Assassin), Saurian Spine
     (longsword, Spellblade). The Saurian spear already IS the Z4 Warrior UT (Magma Lance, 0.3.47). Rows ut.<id> (zone-end band + the orange
     trade-off line), utfx.<id> (existing trick words only), utpow.<id> (the build's fit, at least Fabled). Source = the orange bags (elites,
     mini bosses, dungeons - the 10-18 rule, unchanged GearUt.source); no SkyyMobs drop table needed. The 9 SkyyGear-copy vanilla looks leave the random
     bags (the ut28fix2 rule); the Doomed staff (the armory row's look) stays in the bags until SkyyArmory ships Doomcaller (gl1fix). Names are UNVERIFIED (zone lore; Skyy may rename in tools/ut_vanilla.py). Signatures: none new (sig3 / sig5
     rounds) - each row names its later signature in the table only (nothing shown in game, gear.md 2026-10-03).
  4. THE VOID SCYTHE = MYTHIC: Weapon_Battleaxe_Scythe_Void joins gear.mythicItems (the 0.2.16 developer-bow rule: every new copy Mythic, never in
     random bags; a full-boss source comes with the boss / sig5 round - like the Vampire / Bomb / Pull bows).
  5. POOL: Armor_Diving_Crude_* leave the combat bags (a utility set for SkyyFishing / Exploration later; build-time filter). Armor_Wool_* and the
     dev bows unchanged. LOOT_SKIP_07 unchanged (Longsword_Ruined_Giant + Staff_Voidcrystal wait for Skyy's levels; Flamethrower_Scrap = the
     gun rule) - reported, not changed.
  6. ELEMENT POWER TOOLTIP (A2 critic follow-up): the line = GearAug.power() exactly (socketed tiers + 3 per rolled element line, the 0.3.52 G4
     call - harness-checked against power()); the one part the tooltip cannot know (a running Imbue) is now said under it: "Imbue adds +5 Power
     to its element while it runs."
  ONE-TIME UPDATES (PROJECT-RULES 4): migrateUt53 = migrateUt28's code on the U53_ block (a pure ADDITION of the 30 ut / utfx / utpow rows the
  file lacks; utpow rows skipped when utline.power is an admin value); migrateMy53 = migrateAs51's code on gear.mythicItems (only the untouched
  0.3.52 line -> + Weapon_Battleaxe_Scythe_Void). Both: verified History copy first, a change-log row per entry (Undo), a run-once marker, bytes +
  line endings kept. No new class / command / system; SAVED DATA: none (config only).
  ROLLBACK to 0.3.52: the 9 new copies become unknown items (never roll back once one exists in a player's hands, the Vault or a chest). No Undo
  is needed for the rows (0.3.52 warns once and ignores ut rows of ids it lacks); gear.mythicItems keeps the Void Scythe (0.3.52 reads it the
  same way: Mythic, out of the bags) - Undo it in Server Setup -> Changes for 0.3.52's exact behaviour. The new recipes vanish with the jar
  (crafted Bronze weapons / spears stay normal items). For a clean file restore the History snapshot "before the 0.3.53 Untiered items update".
'''

P = G.Patch(os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyGear", "build_skyygear_0.3.52.py"), os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyGear", "build_skyygear_0.3.53.py"))
